        "The Extended Essay is a 4,000-word independent research paper with a school supervisor and scheduled reflection meetings; TOK carries an exhibition and a 1,600-word essay on a prescribed title. Both reward early, unglamorous decisions — a research question answerable from sources genuinely reachable in Indonesia or online, and a source list built before the school year's midpoint rather than scrambled together after. Many Indonesian SPK schools carry smaller libraries than long-established international schools elsewhere, so planning around what a student can actually access matters more here than a generic reading list assumes.",
